# Keep-warm (self-host stopgap, README "Cold starts"). celld retires a stateless Worker isolate
# that has been idle for about 8 s, and the next request waits 1.5-2.2 s while a new one loads
# the bundle. Caddy's active health check sends GET /health to celld every
# SAM_KEEP_WARM_INTERVAL (default 5s, below celld's idle threshold) for as long as Caddy runs.
#
# The check lives on a route that never matches a request (`expression false`): an active
# health check runs for every provisioned reverse_proxy whether or not traffic reaches it, and
# its verdict only gates this unused route, so a failed or slow /health can never take the real
# proxy below out of service. /health reads no storage and is excluded from SAM's request log.
# Health checks are not requests to the site, so they do not appear in the access log.
#
# Upstream: drop this once celld can keep isolates warm itself (tasks/backlog/
# 2026-11-11-selfhost-celld-isolate-cold-start-slow-page-loads.md).
@sam_keep_warm expression false
handle @sam_keep_warm {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:{$CELLD_PORT:8080} {
		health_uri /health
		health_interval {$SAM_KEEP_WARM_INTERVAL:5s}
		health_timeout 10s
		health_headers {
			# celld builds request.url from X-Forwarded-Host (CELLD_TRUST_FORWARDED_HEADERS=1);
			# /health is routed on the API host.
			Host api.{$SAM_DOMAIN}
			X-Forwarded-Host api.{$SAM_DOMAIN}
			X-Forwarded-Proto https
		}
	}
}
